# Security

- Never put credentials or secrets in source code.
- Local JWT for development; Cognito adapter for future AWS.
- Tenant isolation and branch-level authorization on every request.
- Deny-by-default governance policies.
- Append-only audit logs; ordinary users cannot modify them.
- Secure file uploads; no default retention of raw camera feeds.
- Prompt-injection defenses for agent/tool paths.
- Do not log passwords, API keys, or sensitive personal data.
- Settings APIs must not expose secrets.
